      "id": 1,
      "text": "Finneytown takes its name from Ebenezer Ward Finney, a Revolutionary War soldier whose burial site lies just south of the township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finneytown%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1795, Reverend Ebenezer Ward purchased the land that would become Finneytown from John Cleves Symmes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finneytown%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original settlement sat on a heavily wooded hillside near the Millcreek River, close to the early Ludlow Station blockhouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
